<!--
  Which USB devices offer to open RotorLens.

  Matched by CLASS, not by vendor and product ID:

    class    8   Mass Storage
    subclass 6   SCSI transparent command set
    protocol 80  Bulk-Only Transport   (0x50, written here in decimal)

  That is what a flight controller enumerates as in mass-storage mode, and it
  covers every board rather than the two whose IDs happen to be known here. It
  also covers an SD card reader, which is the import path for pilots whose
  controller logs to a removable card instead of onboard dataflash.

  A vendor filter was the alternative and was rejected: it would have needed the
  VID and PID of each board in MSC mode, would silently fail on any controller
  nobody had tested, and gains nothing — the class triple is exactly the set of
  devices this app has any use for.
-->
<resources>
    <usb-device class="8" subclass="6" protocol="80" />
</resources>
